configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.allowDefaults=Allow Defaults
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.allowDefaults.tooltip=While enabled, this setting allows a default set of blocks to be fluidloggable. Other mods may also add their own blocks.\n§c§lOnly disable this setting if you really know what you're doing!\nThe full set of default fluidloggable blocks added by Fluidlogged API can be viewed on its source page, linked below (click anywhere)\nhttps://github.com/jbredwards/Fluidlogged-API
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.bucketFluidlogging=Bucket Fluidlogging
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.bucketFluidlogging.tooltip=This setting controls how sneaking affects the player's ability to fluidlog blocks with a bucket.\n- Always: Players are always able to fluidlog blocks, regardless of whether they're sneaking. This is the Vanilla 1.13+ behavior.\n- No Sneak: Players cannot fluidlog blocks while sneaking. This is the legacy Fluidlogged API (pre-v3.0.0) behavior.\n- On Sneak: Players can only fluidlog blocks while sneaking.
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.bucketFluidlogging.ALWAYS=Always
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.bucketFluidlogging.NO_SNEAK=No Sneak
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.bucketFluidlogging.ON_SNEAK=On Sneak
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.downloadModConfigs=Community Configs Mode
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.downloadModConfigs.tooltip=This setting controls how the online configs are handled.\n- Disabled: Prevents Fluidlogged API from updating its internal online config cache, and prevents it from being used in-game.\n- Ignore Updates: Prevents Fluidlogged API from updating its internal online config cache, but still allows the existing cache to be applied in-game.\n- Keep Updated: Allows Fluidlogged API to keep its internal online config cache up-to-date, and allows it to be applied in-game.\n§eSee the following link for more info (click anywhere)\nhttps://github.com/jbredwards/Fluidlogged-API-Configs
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.downloadModConfigs.DISABLED=Disabled
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.downloadModConfigs.IGNORE_UPDATES=Ignore Updates
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.downloadModConfigs.KEEP_UPDATED=Keep Updated
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.fancyFluidEntityCollision=Fancy Fluid Collision Mode
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.fancyFluidEntityCollision.tooltip=While enabled, fluid blocks have significantly more accurate collision with entities.\n- Never: Fancy fluid collision is never applied.\n§2  - Performance impact: None\n- Player Entities: Only apply fancy fluid collision to player entities.\n§2  - Performance impact: Negligible\n- Medium Entities: Only apply fancy fluid collision to medium-sized entities (whose bounding box has no side greater than 3 blocks).\n§2  - Performance impact: Small to Medium\n- Always: Universally apply fancy fluid collision to all entities (this should never be used).\n§2  - Performance impact: Small to Very Large
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.fancyFluidEntityCollision.ALWAYS=Always
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.fancyFluidEntityCollision.MEDIUM=Medium Entities
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.fancyFluidEntityCollision.NEVER=Never
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.fancyFluidEntityCollision.PLAYERS=Player Entities
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.fancyFluidRenderer=Fancy Vanilla Fluid Rendering
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.fancyFluidRenderer.tooltip=While enabled, force water and lava to use the same fluid renderer that modded fluids use.\nThis setting has a Medium to Large performance impact, but this can almost always be fixed by using certain optimization mods, like CensoredASM, Nothirium, and VintageFix.\n§eThis setting should only be disabled as a last resort, as it fixes MANY bugs, primarily:\n- MC-4533: §7§oWater and lava graphical glitch when connecting diagonally\n- MC-100886: §7§oFalling sand with an ID of water or lava does not render\n- MC-127030: §7§oWater and lava attempt to connect to fluidlogged blocks when they shouldn't, causing several issues\n- MC-127270: §7§oVisual water and lava level inside fluidlogged blocks do not adjust correctly\n- MC-227302: §7§oSmooth lighting does not work properly on the water surface
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.fixBadFluidMixing=Fix https://bugs.mojang.com/browse/MC-127108
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.fixBadFluidMixing.tooltip=While enabled, waterlogged blocks cannot turn lava into obsidian or cobblestone on physically unconnected sides.\nThis fix is also applied to many modded fluid interactions. Please submit a bug report to Fluidlogged API's issue tracker if you find any incompatible mods!
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.fluidStateIsFireInsulator=Fluids Protect Against Fire
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.fluidStateIsFireInsulator.tooltip=While enabled, flammable blocks cannot ignite while fluidlogged with fireproof fluids.
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.ignoreLowFluidCollision=Prevent Shallow Fluid Swimming
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.ignoreLowFluidCollision.tooltip=While enabled, non-aquatic entities cannot swim in shallow fluids (like in Vanilla 1.13+).\nThis setting stacks with "Fancy Fluid Collision Mode", and has no performance impact while enabled.
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.lavalogVaporizeFlammable=Lava Vaporizing Mode
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.lavalogVaporizeFlammable.tooltip=While enabled, any lava-like fluid (has the lava material) flowing into a flammable block will cause the block to be vaporized.\n- Never: This setting is disabled.\n- Flammable (Fluidloggable): Vaporize flammable blocks that can be fluidlogged.\n- Flammable (All): Vaporize blocks that are flammable.
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.lavalogVaporizeFlammable.FLAMMABLE=Flammable (All)
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.lavalogVaporizeFlammable.FLUIDLOGGABLE=Flammable (Fluidloggable)
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.lavalogVaporizeFlammable.NEVER=Never
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.nonSourceFluidlogging=Non-Source Fluidlogging
configgui.fluidlogged_api.general.nonSourceFluidlogging.tooltip=While enabled, allow fluids that are not source blocks to be fluidloggable.

